1 GOVAX

   govax is an emulator of a DEC VAX running VMS, written in Go: a VAX
   processor with its memory, and the VMS a user-mode program sees (system
   services, RMS files on ODS-2 volumes, DCL, the run-time libraries,
   processes), with MACRO, LINK, LIBRARY, a FORTRAN compiler, and the
   debugger.  Programs built on a real VAX run on it, and programs built
   on it run on a real VAX.

   Start with HELP HINTS, and see the manual, docs/MANUAL.md, in the
   source repository.

